":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nI'm building Godot editor myself using `scons platform=windows target=release_debug tools=yes` \n- Reproducible in Godot 3.7.0-dev.1 (a117d512b00f1646db174e703e7e888519b64608)\n- Not reproducible in Godot 3.6.2 (3cd3caab6779a7f3ec3bbeb9f200db50c735cfc8)\n\nThis is not reproducible with the official 3.7.0-dev.1 build if I don't specify any `Custom Template` in the export settings.\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen running the game with my manually compiled version of Godot 3.7.0-dev.1 in `release`, it crashes.  \n\nWhen doing the same in `release_debug`, I get the following errors:\n```\nERROR: Condition \"!instance\" is true. Returned: Variant()\n   at: MethodBind1<class CanvasItemMaterial,enum CanvasItemMaterial::BlendMode>::call (C:\\Projects\\godot\\core\\method_bind.gen.inc:838) - Condition \"!instance\" is true. Returned: Variant()\n```\n\n[godot.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31551249/godot.log)\n\nThose errors do not happen if I use a manually compiled version of Godot 3.6.2.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Fork Godot at commit `a117d512b00f1646db174e703e7e888519b64608`\n2. Compile runtime with `scons platform=windows target=release tools=no`\n3. Export a game with this compiled runtime \n4. Launch the game and observe the crash after some times\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nI'm not sure how to have a minimal project to reproduce this issue.","closed_by":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{